{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 so only root and opsadmin can use crontab. The policy survived a verified node restart; RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8 remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created the opsadmin account.","Created /etc/cron.allow with exactly root and opsadmin, root:root ownership, mode 0600, and the correct SELinux context.","Verified root and opsadmin can install crontabs while nobody is denied.","Removed all temporary verification crontabs.","Safely restarted node1 once and verified recovery and persistence."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin may schedule cron jobs","command_ids":["cmd-e5606733786349fb","cmd-2fe6b661f04646e8","cmd-ed5f58912a6143b0","cmd-ba0750a13cc143c7","cmd-34dc21b017e64e46"],"summary":"The account and exact allowlist are present. Functional tests before and after restart allowed root and opsadmin and rejected nobody. Final crontab spool is clean."},{"requirement":"Preserve installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-9f109588d683453b","cmd-34dc21b017e64e46"],"summary":"Before and after changes, node1 reports RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-508c0e59a416456b","cmd-7300b23b1060425c","cmd-e66c4e9ebc984ccf","cmd-d6db4c7e9717481d","cmd-ba0750a13cc143c7","cmd-34dc21b017e64e46"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 377b5195-7fea-4219-a67b-044ef3f7ab99 was captured, reboot acknowledged, and the new boot ID 02d652b4-c542-4ede-8f97-257e6fc81dcf observed. The system returned to running, crond became active, and functional cron access controls persisted."}]}
